WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:35.190 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  almost two years ago i uploaded a video  titled  who are the hunters and like everything  i've produced up until now  it was just something that interested me  very little was discussed about them in  the game  so after researching everything that i  could find on them i realized that i  wasn't alone with these questions  there were so many active theories on  them but most didn't line up with my  understanding of the story at that point  so i decided to pull together some of  the larger theories out there including  a few of my own  and talk about the likelihood of each of  them i had no idea that others would  find this as interesting as i did  it was only my second lore video and  this one was more speculation than law  itself  a little under a year later i released  an update to this video  talking to some of the feedback  considering the first video but also a  number of new theories that had come up  since the release of the division 2.  and here we are today another 12 months  on this video is more of a small  update to the series of videos that have  been running for the last two years  unfortunately the hunters have taken an  odd turn in the story since they were  first released in the survival expansion  of the original game  the hunters seem to have become more of  a puzzle element to the game than part  of the story  so there isn't actually a huge amount  more that we have to work with  however thanks to one keynote member on  discord there may be a little something  more that we have to go on  i receive hundreds of theories and  images every month from people  interested in finding out more about the  division story  most of them i've seen or talked about  before but every now and then  something catches me by surprise a  discord user that goes by the name of  monarch sent me some information he'd  been compiling regarding the new hunters  that we were finding after the release  of warlords of new york  i'll be the first to admit i wasn't  hugely excited at first but then he sent  me through this image  this is a picture of warlords of new  york hunter angel  while this alone may not seem very  significant over time monarch sent me  more images like this  from other hunters he was able to take  down time and time again  the same tattoo so what does this mean  it could mean absolutely nothing these  could just be duplicated models  with zero significance around the tattoo  but the devs and ubisoft games love  leaving little tidbits and clues around  that could lead to a greater story so we  investigated further  fortunately monarch used to be part of a  us milsim role play group  and had some knowledge in this area but  also has a contact with ties to the army  on top of this i ran this past a number  of other people with experience in the  area  including twitter user james hurt their  conclusions were all the same  a lot of military tattoos represent the  brotherhood they had in their time of  service  or are from a certain battle that he or  she lost friends in  or it could be something more personal  to the individual  but there appears to be military ranks  on either side and there was no  variation  between each hunter they confirmed these  as u.s army ranks  or more specifically united states army  first sergeant  private and private first class  i went back through my footage of  division 1 hunters and the first hunters  seen in the division 2  some of which is playing on screen right  now but in both cases  their arms seem to be covered down to  the forearm so i couldn't confirm that  they too have the same tattoos  but i have since found a number of  images to the earlier division 2 hunters  who do have these  a first class sergeant serves as a  senior enlisted advisor to the commander  of a medium to large unit of marines  such as a platoon or company as the  senior enlisted advisor  first sergeants hold the responsibility  of being the main bridge between  enlisted marines  and their company commander they may be  united states special operations command  or more specifically either delta force  seals special operations group  or green berets but they also could be a  black ops unit  special operations group or green braise  can operate alone due to the nature of  their missions  if the hunters are in fact from these  units within the military this could  explain the reason behind the guerrilla  warfare tactics  and how they combat other units and why  they dress in plain clothes  could even coincide to other links  within the tom clancy universe like the  ghosts  or rainbow six private military  contractors are often made up of people  with previous military experience so  it's no surprise to see that a number of  black tusks are also sporting tattoos  however what is surprising is the number  of black tusks who have exactly the same  tattoo as the hunters  all the way down to the ranks and the  image in the centre  riflemen bernadieres engineers the  bosses in the invaded capitol hill and  viewpoint museum missions  even brenner  so what does this all mean well it tells  us a couple of things  the hunters originated from the us or at  the very least come from a u.s military  background  yes you could loosely theorise that the  russians had them get these tattoos to  provide them some sort of undercover  illusion that they are americans  but the earlier hunters didn't even show  them and to have the exact same tattoos  as the black tusk  seems unlikely so i'm going to discredit  the hunters are russian special forces  theory for now it also seems to show  that they have some sort of ties to the  black tusk  at the very least they come from the  same u.s military unit  but they could in fact be a part of the  black tusk the black tusk we come across  in the division are from a more  specialized branch of the overall  company called the btsu  or black tusk special unit maybe the  hunters are a special unit within the  special unit  the black tusk super special unit if you  like  or what if they attempted to gain  employment through the black tusk with  the rest of their squad  but were deemed too aggressive or  generally unsuitable for the general  cohesion of one of their specialist  units  and they were instead brought on as a  hired gun to take out former and current  division agents  this actually may explain their  obsession with collecting agent watches  these are essentially their paycheck  however this doesn't exactly write off  the third wave or contingency theory  either  the hunters are obviously highly trained  forces particularly in guerilla warfare  tactics  they use the same tech as the division  if not slightly better  and as far as the tattoo goes maybe they  just have a similar history to the black  tusk  but took a different direction after the  time in the military  i realize this has probably only raised  even more questions  but this has given us a little more to  work with given the direction that the  hunters have taken since the division  one there really hasn't been too much to  work with  let's face it when we think about the  hunter's involvement in the story up  until this point  basically they've become nothing more  than a puzzle to solve in order to  acquire a new mask  and i do wonder if we had been given  their full story by now  would they have long since faded into  oblivion  but at this point i want to hand this  over to you what do you think this  tattoo means  is there anything else you can share on  the hunters that could lead to further  theories on their origins and objectives  personally i'm wanting to dig a little  deeper into someone that we saved early  on in dc  vikram malik i think there is a lot more  to the story  and i've seen enough to think that he  could have some sort of involvement with  the hunters  but time will tell otherwise i must  thank monarch for his research on this  and all the information he provided  and also james hurt for his feedback  thanks again for watching and i'll catch  you in the next one  [Music]  cheers  [Music]  uh

